  {
    id: 'm9',
    title: 'A Letter to My Future Self',
    type: '书信',
    level: '中考',
    words: 129,
    prompt: '假定你是李华，中考前一年，请给一年后的自己写一封信，谈谈你现在的学习与期待。',
    essay: [
      'Dear Future Me,',
      'It is a rainy Sunday evening, and there are twelve months left before the entrance exam. I am writing to ask whether you kept the promises I make tonight.',
      'My life now is simple but busy. I have six classes every morning and forty minutes of maths each night, because maths is still my weakest subject. Even so, small efforts make a difference day after day.',
      'I hope two good things stand behind you. First, that you kept the reading habit and filled one more notebook. Second, that you are calmer than I am, because I still get nervous before tests.',
      'Whatever result you get, please be proud of yourself. If you have worked hard, you are the person I hope to become.',
      'Yours,',
      'Li Hua',
    ],
    zh: [
      '亲爱的未来的我：',
      '这是一个下雨的星期日夜晚，距离中考正好还有十二个月。我写这封信，是想问你：我今晚许下的承诺，你都守住了吗？',
      '我现在的生活简单而忙碌。每天上午六节课，晚上再做四十分钟数学，因为数学仍是我最弱的科目。即便如此，小小的努力日复一日地重复，也会带来改变。',
      '希望你身后站着两件好事。第一，你保持了阅读的习惯，又写满了一本笔记。第二，你比现在的我更从容，因为我每次考试前仍然会紧张。',
      '无论结果如何，都请为自己骄傲。只要你努力过，你就是我希望成为的那个人。',
      '祝好，',
      '李华',
    ],
    expressions: ['make a difference', 'day after day', 'calmer than I am', 'Whatever result you get', 'be proud of yourself', 'the person I hope to become'],
  },

  {
    id: 'm10',
    title: 'The Broken Crown',
    type: '记叙',
    level: '中考',
    words: 129,
    prompt: '你们小组为班级准备英语短剧，演出前却出了岔子。请叙述这次活动如何搞砸又被补救成功，并谈谈你的感受。',
    essay: [
      'Last month our group prepared an English play for the class, and I was in charge of the props.',
      'On the morning of the show, I found our box empty. My brother had taken out the paper swords and the king\'s crown, which came back broken in half. We had only two hours left.',
      'We acted at once. Two classmates drew new swords on cardboard while I glued the crown with tape. Then our leader changed the ending, so the broken crown became a joke in the story.',
      'Our play won second prize, and our teacher said the damaged crown was the best part. I learned that a bad moment is not the end of the road. If you stay calm, you can turn it into a good one.',
    ],
    zh: [
      '上个月，我们小组为班级准备一场英语短剧，我负责道具。',
      '演出当天早上，我发现道具箱是空的。弟弟把纸剑和国王皇冠都拿了出去，还回来的皇冠已经断成两半。我们只剩两个小时了。',
      '我们立刻行动。两个同学用硬纸板画出新剑，我用胶带把皇冠粘了回去。随后组长改了结尾，让这顶破皇冠成了故事里的笑点。',
      '最后我们的短剧拿了二等奖，老师说那顶破皇冠是全剧最好的地方。我由此明白，糟糕的一刻并不是路的尽头；只要稳住神，你就能把它变成好的时刻。',
    ],
    expressions: ['in charge of', 'acted at once', 'broken in half', 'became a joke in the story', 'the best part', 'not the end of the road'],
  },

  {
    id: 'm11',
    title: 'New Time for Our English Corner',
    type: '通知',
    level: '中考',
    words: 129,
    prompt: '你是学生会成员李华。原定本周六上午的学校英语角因故改期，请写一则通知，告知新的时间、地点和注意事项。',
    essay: [
      'May I have your attention, please?',
      'Here is a notice about our English Corner. It was to be held in the school hall at nine on Saturday morning. Because the hall is being repaired, it will now take place from four to five on Wednesday afternoon, in the reading area of the library.',
      'This time our topic is My Favourite Festival, and the first three students who speak will get a small prize. Please remember three things. First, prepare a self-introduction of about three minutes. Second, try to speak English and do not be afraid of making mistakes. Third, no food or drinks, so that we can keep the reading area clean.',
      'Anyone who is interested can sign up with our English teacher before Friday noon.',
      'The Student Union',
    ],
    zh: [
      '请大家注意一下，好吗？',
      '这里有一则关于英语角的通知。活动原定周六上午九点在学校礼堂举行；由于礼堂正在维修，现改为本周三下午四点到五点，在图书馆阅览区进行。',
      '这次的话题是“我最喜欢的节日”，最先发言的三位同学会得到一份小奖品。请注意三件事：第一，准备一段约三分钟的自我介绍；第二，尽量说英语，不要怕犯错；第三，请不要带食物和饮料，以便我们保持阅览区干净。',
      '任何感兴趣的同学都可以在周五中午之前到英语老师那里报名。',
      '学生会',
    ],
    expressions: ['May I have your attention, please?', 'Here is a notice about...', 'take place', 'be afraid of making mistakes', 'Anyone who is interested can...', 'sign up with'],
  },

  {
    id: 'm12',
    title: 'Should We Use Electronic Devices Every Day to Study?',
    type: '观点论证',
    level: '高考',
    words: 206,
    prompt: '如今中学生可以很方便地用平板和手机学习。请以“中学生该不该每天使用电子设备学习”为题写一篇短文，阐明观点并说明理由。',
    essay: [
      'Electronic devices have made studying easier, but they have also started an argument worth a closer look. I agree that a tablet can change daily study, yet I believe it should be used every day only with clear rules.',
      'The first benefit is immediate feedback. When I am stuck on an English sentence at eleven at night, a dictionary app explains my mistake and lets me find the problem myself. This keeps me working without a teacher, the skill I need most.',
      'The second benefit is real language. A textbook gives model passages, but a podcast or a video from a student in another country gives a living voice. For those who plan to study abroad, this is especially valuable.',
      'Admittedly, a phone with us every day can distract us, and twenty minutes of review may turn into an hour of games. However, this is an argument against careless use, not against the device. If we keep to one hour in study mode, the problem becomes much smaller.',
      'For these reasons, I am convinced that middle school students may use electronic devices every day, as long as they set a purpose and a limit. No tool makes anyone a good learner; the person using it does.',
    ],
    zh: [
      '电子设备让学习更容易了，却也引发了一个值得细看的争论。我同意平板能够改变每天的学习，但我认为，只有在明确的规则下，它才适合每天使用。',
      '第一个好处是即时反馈。深夜十一点被一个英语句子卡住时，词典应用会指出我的错误，让我自己找到问题。它让我在没有老师的情况下仍能学下去，而这正是我最需要的能力。',
      '第二个好处是真实的语言。课本给我示范的篇章，而播客或另一个国家学生拍的视频给我鲜活的声音。对有留学打算的同学来说，这一点尤其宝贵。',
      '诚然，每天都带在身边的手机会让我们分心，二十分钟的复习可能变成一小时的游戏。然而，这反对的是粗心的使用，而不是设备本身。当我们只在学习模式下用一小时，问题就小得多了。',
      '基于这些理由，我确信中学生可以每天使用电子设备，只要先定好目的和限度。没有哪种工具能把谁变成好的学习者，是使用工具的人做到了这一点。',
    ],
    expressions: ['worth a closer look', 'The first benefit is...', 'the skill I need most', 'Admittedly, ... However, ...', 'an argument against careless use, not against the device', 'For these reasons, I am convinced that...'],
  },

  {
    id: 'm13',
    title: 'An Invitation to Give an Online Lecture on Chinese Culture',
    type: '书信',
    level: '高考',
    words: 181,
    prompt: '假定你是阳光中学学生会李华，请给在你校任教的外籍教授 Smith 写一封邮件，邀请他为全校学生做一场中国文化的线上讲座。',
    essay: [
      'Dear Professor Smith,',
      'I am Li Hua from the Students\' Union, and I am writing on behalf of our school. We would like to invite you to give our students an online lecture on Chinese culture.',
      'The talk would last about forty minutes on Friday afternoon, May 9, on our school platform. You may choose your own topic, yet most of us voted for the one you mentioned after class, because we want to know how Chinese families celebrate the traditional festivals and how young people keep these customs alive.',
      'About three hundred students will join in their own classrooms, and your screen will be shown on the big display in each room, so please speak as if you were talking to one small group. We will also prepare some questions in advance.',
      'If any part of this plan should change, please let me know. We would be grateful if you could give us your answer before April 30, and we are ready to help with the slides and the platform.',
      'Looking forward to hearing from you.',
      'Yours sincerely,',
      'Li Hua',
    ],
    zh: [
      '尊敬的 Smith 教授：',
      '我是学生会李华，谨代表我们学校给您写信。我们想邀请您为全校学生做一场关于中国文化的线上讲座。',
      '讲座长约四十分钟，定于5月9日周五下午在我们学校的平台上进行。主题可以由您决定，不过大多数同学投票选了您课后提到的那个，因为我们想知道中国家庭如何庆祝传统节日，年轻人今天又如何让这些习俗保持活力。',
      '大约三百名同学会在自己的教室接入，您的画面会投送到每间教室的大屏幕上，所以请您像面对一个小组那样自然地讲述。我们也会提前准备一些问题。',
      '如果这个安排有任何需要调整之处，请告诉我。若您能在4月30日前回复，我们将不胜感激；我们也随时可以协助制作幻灯片和测试平台。',
      '期待您的回复。',
      '此致',
      '李华',
    ],
    expressions: ['I am writing on behalf of...', 'We would like to invite you to...', 'You may choose your own topic, yet...', 'in advance', 'We would be grateful if you could...', 'Looking forward to hearing from you.'],
  },

  {
    id: 'm14',
    title: 'What Failure Taught Us',
    type: '演讲稿',
    level: '高考',
    words: 204,
    prompt: '毕业典礼上，请你就“失败的价值”发表一篇演讲，结合自己的经历谈谈你从失败中学到了什么。',
    essay: [
      'Good morning, teachers, parents and classmates. It is an honour to speak on our graduation day, and today I would like to talk about the value of failure.',
      'I did not learn this lesson from a book. Last summer I spent the whole of June preparing for a maths exam, and I improved by only five points. I was so ashamed that I could not look at the paper again. Yet those five points told me something useful, because I had been solving the questions I understood and avoiding the ones I did not.',
      'Failure also has a public side. Edison tested thousands of materials before the light bulb worked, and he said each one taught him a way that did not work. In other words, failure collects knowledge long before it collects praise.',
      'We often fear failure because school makes it feel like a full stop. It is actually a comma, because it marks the place where something must be changed.',
      'As we leave these gates, I will not promise that everything will go well. I will promise that when it goes badly, I will stay long enough to find out why. That is the gift failure gives us.',
      'Thank you for listening.',
    ],
    zh: [
      '老师们、家长们、同学们，大家上午好。能在毕业典礼上发言我深感荣幸，今天我想谈谈失败的价值。',
      '这堂课不是书本教给我的。去年夏天，我花了整个六月准备一场数学考试，成绩却只提高了五分。我羞愧得再也无法看那张卷子。然而正是这五分告诉了我一件有用的事：我一直在做自己已经懂的题，而躲开了不懂的那些。',
      '失败也有它公共的一面。爱迪生在电灯成功之前测试了上千种材料，而他说每一种都教会了他一条行不通的路。换句话说，失败在收获赞誉之前，早就在积累知识。',
      '我们常常害怕失败，因为学校让它看起来像一个句号。它其实是一个逗号，因为它标出了必须改变的地方。',
      '走出这扇大门时，我不会向大家保证一切顺利。我保证的是：当事情不顺时，我会停留足够长的时间，去弄清楚为什么。这就是失败给我们的礼物。',
      '谢谢大家的聆听。',
    ],
    expressions: ['I would like to talk about...', 'I did not learn this lesson from a book.', 'In other words, ...', 'a full stop... a comma', 'As we leave these gates, ...', 'Thank you for listening.'],
  },

  {
    id: 'm15',
    title: 'The Last Metre',
    type: '读后续写',
    level: '高考',
    words: 203,
    prompt: '原文大意：爷爷年轻时是游泳健将，陈浩从小在县城老泳池跟他学游泳。爷爷病倒后泳池关了，他只送给孙子一副旧泳镜，说过一句“别只想着赢”。暑假城市游泳赛，陈浩第一次进入决赛。续写要求：第一段必须以 Ten metres to go, and the boy in the next lane was still three lengths ahead. 开头；第二段必须以 At that moment, the memory of Grandpa teaching him in the old pool came back. 开头，两段之间要有情节推进，并与原文的旧泳镜和爷爷的教导形成情感呼应。',
    essay: [
      'Ten metres to go, and the boy in the next lane was still three lengths ahead. The water seemed to slow Chen Hao down, and the noise of the hall became one long roar. For a second he thought about giving up, because losing here was painful enough. Then he saw his own reflection in the dark water, and he remembered the old goggles with the same crack across the lens.',
      'At that moment, the memory of Grandpa teaching him in the old pool came back. Grandpa had stood in the deep end and told him to stop fighting the water. "Breathe, count four, then pull, and do not look at the others," he had shouted. So Chen Hao stopped looking. He counted four and pulled one more time. When he touched the wall, the board showed first, and the roar came back to his ears.',
      'Later that evening, Chen Hao called Grandpa and told him the race, metre by metre. Grandpa laughed and said that a medal was only a piece of metal unless it made you remember something. Before he hung up, he asked his grandson to wear the old goggles tomorrow, because the river behind the house was still waiting.',
    ],
    zh: [
      '还剩十米，邻道的男孩仍然领先三个身位。水似乎在拖慢陈浩，全场的声响汇成一片长长的轰鸣。他有一瞬间想过放弃，因为在这里输掉已经够难受了。随后他看见深水里自己的倒影，想起那副旧泳镜，镜片上也有着一道同样的裂缝。',
      '就在那一刻，爷爷在老泳池教他游泳的记忆涌了回来。爷爷站在深水区，叫他别再和水较劲。“吸气，数四下，再划水，别看别人！”他当时这样喊道。于是陈浩不再去看别人。他数了四下，最后一次划水。触壁时，计分板上他是第一，轰鸣声重新灌进耳朵。',
      '那天晚上，陈浩给爷爷打了电话，把比赛一米一米地讲给他听。爷爷笑着说，奖牌不过是一块金属，除非它能让你想起一些东西。挂电话前，他让孙子明天戴上那副旧泳镜，因为屋后那条河还在等他。',
    ],
    expressions: ['Ten metres to go, ...', 'For a second... Then...', 'At that moment, ... came back', 'the memory of... came back', 'metre by metre', 'unless it made you remember something'],
  },

  {
    id: 'm16',
    title: 'A Proposal on Saving Food at School',
    type: '倡议书',
    level: '高考',
    words: 195,
    prompt: '学校食堂每天倒掉大量饭菜。请以学生会的名义写一篇倡议书，指出校园食物浪费问题，并向全体同学发出具体可行的行动号召。',
    essay: [
      'Dear fellow students,',
      'Please look at the bins outside our canteen for one minute. Last term our school weighed the food thrown away every day, and the result was nearly one ton for the whole school. Waste is therefore not a small habit we were born with; it is a choice, and a choice can be changed.',
      'The change should begin with what we can actually do. Take a little less rice at first, and go back if you are still hungry. If you cannot finish a dish, share it with a friend instead of leaving it on the tray. When a meal does not taste right, tell the canteen staff politely and ask them to change the menu.',
      'Our class can do more than this. We plan to check clean plates every Wednesday, put up posters designed by students, and work with a community food bank.',
      'Saving food is not a slogan on a wall. It is a decision we make three times a day, and it shows what we think of the land, the water and the hands that grew our meal. Let us start today, with our own trays.',
      'The Students\' Union',
    ],
    zh: [
      '亲爱的同学们：',
      '请到我们食堂外的泔水桶前看上一分钟。上学期学校称量了每天倒掉的食物，全校一天接近一吨。因此，浪费并不是我们生来就有的小习惯，而是一种选择；既然是选择，就可以改变。',
      '改变应当从我们真正能做的事开始。起初少盛一点米饭，还饿再添。一道菜吃不完时，请和朋友分着吃，而不是留在餐盘里。饭菜口味不对时，请礼貌地告诉食堂工作人员，请他们更换菜单。',
      '我们能做的还不止于此。我们打算每周三检查光盘情况，张贴由同学设计的海报，并与社区食物银行合作。',
      '节约食物不是墙上的口号，而是我们每天做出三次的决定；它显示出我们如何看待脚下的土地、灌溉的水和种出这顿饭的那双手。就从今天开始，从我们自己的餐盘开始。',
      '学生会',
    ],
    expressions: ['Please look at... for one minute.', 'it is a choice, and a choice can be changed', 'The change should begin with...', 'instead of', 'do more than this', 'not a slogan on a wall'],
  },
